.git/
/data/
docs/*
!docs/connector-contract.md
!docs/style-guide.md
# ^ tests/hub/test_first_screens_e3.py reads the style guide's dated supersession line (gate FAILED on the NAS 2026-10-14)
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
# Secrets: `*` does not cross `/`, so the ** forms are needed to catch deploy/.env (review D-01)
**/.env
**/*.env
!**/*.env.example
# NAS one-shot backups of .env / edge.env (nas_scripts/*.sh) can carry secrets, e.g. deploy/edge.env.bak-<date>-<HHMM>
**/*.bak-*
deploy/history.log
# the running deploy writes its log here while `docker build .` reads the context
deploy/logs/
.preview/
drop/
connectors/money/samples/
connectors/money/golden_local/
# Joey TV shell (WP-B7/B8): the Android project never enters the life-test image, including the public debug p12.
# The gate reads only the three release-metadata files (tests/tv/test_version_file.py, tests/deploy/test_tv_context.py).
tv/*
!tv/VERSION
!tv/NOTES.txt
!tv/SIGNING_CERT_SHA256
